# ─── Quartus build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Regenerated by every compile. The submission ZIP forbids "files that are not
# relevant for compilation or a result of compilation", so none of this belongs
# in the deliverable either.
db/
incremental_db/
output_files/
simulation/
greybox_tmp/
hc_output/
hps_isw_handoff/
*.qws
*.rpt
*.summary
*.smsg
*.pin
*.done
*.jdi
*.qdf
*.sld
*.dpf
*.bak
*.orig

# NOTE: *.sof is deliberately NOT ignored. Quartus writes it into output_files/,
# which is ignored, so each final SOF must be copied by hand into
# Quartus/RV32IMscMCU/ or Quartus/RV32IMpipelinedMCU/ to reach the submission.

# ─── ModelSim / Questa ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
work/
transcript
*.wlf
wlf*
vsim.dbg
vsim_stacktrace.vstf
*.cr.mti
.modelsim

# Intermediate produced inside mem_dump.do and deleted at the end of it; only
# present if a run was interrupted mid-dump.
DTCM_raw.mem

# NOTE: DTCM.mem is NOT ignored. It is the artefact compared against the RARS
# golden DTCM.h, so a captured run should be committed under a name that says
# which test produced it, e.g. DTCM_test3.mem.

# ─── RARS / toolchain scratch ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.o
*.elf
*.lst

# ─── Claude Code ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local agent settings and permissions. Not relevant for compilation, so it also
# does not belong in the submission ZIP.
.claude/

# ─── OS and editor ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
~$*
*~
*.swp
